---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <main class="main-container py-12">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The mind, the model, and the signal</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 via-white to-sky-50 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-900/80 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-slate-900/70">
      <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
        I am a researcher, teacher, and engineer interested in how intelligent systems can help us understand the brain, decode complex signals, and support meaningful clinical decisions. My work sits at the intersection of <span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">AI</span>, <span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">computational neuroscience</span>, and <span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">data-driven science</span>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-300">Brain and AI</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">NeuroAI</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          I am fascinated by the relationship between intelligence and the brain: how neural dynamics can inspire better learning systems, and how modern AI can help reveal structure in cognitive and clinical data. My interest in NeuroAI is not only technical, but also philosophical: how we model cognition, perception, and reasoning through data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-300">Signal processing</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">EEG and clinical intelligence</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          My research focuses on electroencephalography and patient-level predictive modeling, especially for neurological outcome prediction after cardiac arrest. I work with EEG preprocessing, representation learning, experimental design, and foundation-model transfer to understand how information from the brain can support clinically meaningful prediction systems.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/80">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300">Motivation</p>
      <blockquote class="mt-4 text-2xl font-medium leading-relaxed text-slate-800 italic dark:text-slate-100">
        “Knowledge is not born from certainty; it is born from the courage to question, learn, and seek the hidden order behind the signal.”
      </blockquote>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">— Sebastián Yepes</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">Research philosophy</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        I believe that good science is both rigorous and humane. The goal is not only to build models that predict, but to build systems that can help us understand uncertainty, improve decisions, and make technology useful for people. That is the thread connecting my work in teaching, algorithms, privacy, and biomedical modeling.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
